# Drafted by Gemini (R14 flames), edited.

~ pyre_start
set night_of_flames_active
if not quest.crimson_monastery >= night_of_flames
quest crimson_monastery night_of_flames
endif
cutscene mon_flames
Narrator: Sixty faithful in red robes ring the cold stones round six captives tied to pitch-soaked stakes. Friar Olaf paces below with a guttering torch while Father Renathyr watches from the high stair.
* Watch in silence. -> pyre_watch
* Call out to Gareth to recant. -> urge_start
* Cry out against the burning and push forward. -> force_stop

~ pyre_watch
approve tobin_hayward -4 silas_vane -3 lucan_houndstooth -2: You stood silent while Gareth Creed burned at the stake
friar_olaf [smile]: Hear me, children, for my voice is the last mercy you shall know tonight. Name the Crimson Rose your lady, and these kind hands shall untie your cords.
Narrator: Five captives weep the words and stumble free as the ropes fall away. Only Gareth remains, shaking his head while Olaf lowers the torch.
gareth_creed [afraid]: The morning song is mine to keep. I will not give you my voice.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep my burlap three paces back from that torch, or we all go up together.
friar_olaf [angry]: Ask again, stubborn lamb, while you still have a tongue to spend.
gareth_creed [angry]: Never.
cutscene mon_flames_2
cutscene mon_flames_3
set gareth_fate = "burned"
Narrator: Black silhouettes twist behind a wall of roaring gold, and then nothing remains on the night wind but bitter sulfur and a heavy, ringing silence.
-> pyre_end

~ urge_start
Narrator: Father Renathyr lifts one gloved hand on the stair, and sixty hooded heads turn toward you in the hush.
father_renathyr [neutral]: Peace, friends. The fire asks its own question, and no man may answer for another.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Plead that we are new converts who only wish to help a brother. -> urge_ok | urge_miss
* [Deception DC 20] Say we are Gareth's cousins and know his heart. -> urge_ok | urge_miss
* Stand beside Olaf and recite the creed. -> urge_creed
* Step back. -> pyre_watch

~ urge_miss
father_renathyr [weary]: Your zeal outruns your wisdom, pilgrims. Keep your place, or find a truer way to prove your devotion.
-> urge_start

~ urge_creed
Narrator: You step into the torchlight beside Friar Olaf and speak the Crimson words, and a low murmur of approval ripples through the red robes. On the stair, Father Renathyr inclines his head.
set crimson_devotions += 1
-> urge_ok

~ urge_ok
father_renathyr [smile]: Go on, then. If your words can save a stubborn branch from the winter fire, the Rose will gladly take the bloom.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Urge Gareth to say the words. -> recant | gareth_hold
* [if flag.melina_met] [Persuasion DC 10] Say Melina's name. -> recant | gareth_hold
* [if item:melinas_songbird] Show him Melina's wooden songbird. -> recant
* Step back. -> pyre_watch

~ gareth_hold
Narrator: Gareth sets his jaw and shakes his head against the post, though the torch has not yet touched the brushwood.
gareth_creed [afraid]: Better the ash than a hollow song. Leave me be.
-> urge_ok

~ recant
Narrator: A tremor takes Gareth from boot to shoulder as the five beside him stumble free.
gareth_creed [sad]: The Crimson Rose is my lady. May the birds forgive me.
interject name:silas_vane: Live to deal another hand, friend. A dead man never broke the house bank.
Narrator: The novices cut his cords, and as he rubs his raw wrists he catches your eye, whispering that he will slip back to Wickermoor once the roads are quiet.
set gareth_fate = "rescued"
set crimson_devotions += 1
-> pyre_end

~ force_stop
approve tobin_hayward +3 lucan_houndstooth +2 cordelia_skein -2: You charged a courtyard of sixty zealots to stop the pyre
gate_veteran_cm [angry]: Hold them down! Do not let them near the stakes!
Narrator: Iron hands catch your cloaks, and then the whole red-robed crowd presses in until stone and boot-heels blur into the dark. The captives are hauled back to the wood, and when your head clears, you lie on the frost-rimed flagstones of the Dead Larder.
set gareth_fate = "burned"
set crimson_captured
set night_of_flames_done
set night_of_flames_active
jail mon_ground:larder keep_gear until flag.larder_out
-> END

~ pyre_end
father_renathyr [smile]: Come inside from the mountain chill, my new friends, for there is no blame left in the embers. Easy now, Duchess, they are guests. Pray join me in the cathedral after the Twilight bell.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Velvet gloves and a warm welcome right after a burning. Watch your seams, darlings.
set night_of_flames_done
set crimson_in
set renathyr_invited_cathedral
standing crimson_faith +5
if not quest.crimson_monastery >= inside
quest crimson_monastery inside
endif
-> END

~ pyre_cold
Narrator: The pyre has burned down to cold grey ash, leaving only blackened stakes and a lingering smell of sulfur.
-> END
